/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":433304,"digest":"sha256:ac5bc329d34a4fd1e3ef776cf690fa3a0a0b56f00ed780ce62be64b104cfebe9","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-13T22:49:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T22:49:40Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/mikonyaa/lessonroutes/releases/download/v0.1.1/workspace.lessonroutes.project.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikonyaa/lessonroutes/tarball/v0.1.1","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mikonyaa/lessonroutes/zipball/v0.1.1","body":"LessonRoutes 0.1.1 fixes three local authoring data defects:\n\n- Retired autosaves cannot replace the current project after New/Open/Save a new copy. Saved belongs to the displayed session's committed snapshot; edits made during a save are retained.\n- Startup recovery completes before editing is enabled. Storage timeouts/errors leave an explicit recovery message, memory work and editable backup available.\n- Deleting or reordering actions preserves logical order through undo/redo, project backups, preview and the standalone player, including valid shuffled JSON arrays.\n\nKeyboard action order is consistent across editor and player. Dialogs restore focus after closing. Dependencies and the original image bytes are retained.\n\nSource: `020c20cc81152130cbaaa274e922bdbd687ec9a0`.\nThe ZIP is the unchanged artifact from [Verify LessonRoutes, push/main](https://github.com/mikonyaa/lessonroutes/actions/runs/38479208321): 69 unit tests and 108 browser tests across Chromium, Firefox and Playwright WebKit, plus fresh-ZIP consumer verification.\n\nExtract the web ZIP and run `node serve.mjs` with Node 24. No consumer node_modules are needed. `lesson.html` is the offline learner example; `workspace.lessonroutes.project.json` is its editable backup. Browser recovery is local to its origin and does not replace a portable backup. Checksums and CI provenance are attached.\n\nThe macOS consumer also verifies exact saved hard refresh, root/arbitrary subpath authoring, backup/reimport/export and keyboard completion/restart at 390 px through an isolated offline file URL with persistent storage disabled. All release bytes and the actual Pages editor are checked again after publication.\n\nPhysical touch, manual screen-reader qualification, other platform combinations and independent teacher-to-learner handoffs remain unverified. The product remains experimental.\n"}